    "title": "Geodesic convexity of bags is preserved by un-subdivision",
    "description": "In a tree decomposition where every bag is convex along shortest paths, contracting each subdivided path of a subdivided graph back to a single edge should yield a tree decomposition of the original graph whose bags remain shortest-path convex, with no increase in width. This would prove that the geodesic treewidth of a subdivision is at least that of the original graph. Approach: a subdivided edge is an isometric path, so a geodesically convex bag meets it in a contiguous segment; collapsing the segment to an endpoint preserves convexity because path distances collapse in lockstep with the endpoints. Build on the plain-treewidth collapse map that pushes bags forward along a vertex map that is the identity off the contracted middle vertex.",
